 players of different teams:**\n   Each player shakes hands with every player on the other two teams three times. Since there are 3 teams, each player has a total of \\(8\\) (other players) to shake hands with, and each handshake is done three times.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Handshakes per player with other teams} = 8 \\times 3 = 24\n   \\]\n   Since there are 12 players, and each handshake is counted twice (once for each participant), the total number of these handshakes is:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total handshakes between different teams} = \\frac{12 \\times 24}{2} = 144\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the handshakes between players of the same team:**\n   Each player shakes hands with each of the other 3 players on their own team once.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Handshakes per player with own team} = 3\n   \\]\n   Since there are 12 players, and each handshake is counted twice, the total number of these handshakes is:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total handshakes within the same team} = \\frac{12 \\times 3}{2} = 18\n   \\]\n\n4. **Calculate the total number of handshakes:**\n   Adding the handshakes between different teams and within the same team, we get:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total handshakes} = 144 + 18 = 162\n   \\]\n\nThus, the total number of handshakes is \\(\\boxed{162}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{162}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
